2️⃣ Generate my first embedding

Same packages as Day 8 (Microsoft.Extensions.AI + OllamaSharp).
The interface changes from IChatClient → IEmbeddingGenerator.

csharpusing Microsoft.Extensions.AI;
using OllamaSharp;

IEmbeddingGenerator<string, Embedding<float>> embedder =
    new OllamaApiClient(new Uri("http://localhost:11434"), "nomic-embed-text");

// GenerateVectorAsync = convenience for a single string
ReadOnlyMemory<float> vector = await embedder.GenerateVectorAsync("login failed");

Console.WriteLine($"Dimensions: {vector.Length}"); // e.g. 768
Console.WriteLine($"First 5: {string.Join(", ", vector.ToArray()[..5])}");

That pile of numbers is the meaning of "login failed."
No single number means anything — the pattern across all of them carries the meaning.

3️⃣ The "aha" moment — compare meanings

csharpusing Microsoft.Extensions.AI;
using OllamaSharp;

IEmbeddingGenerator<string, Embedding<float>> embedder =
    new OllamaApiClient(new Uri("http://localhost:11434"), "nomic-embed-text");

float[] a = (await embedder.GenerateVectorAsync("login failed")).ToArray();
float[] b = (await embedder.GenerateVectorAsync("authentication error")).ToArray();
float[] c = (await embedder.GenerateVectorAsync("banana bread recipe")).ToArray();

Console.WriteLine($"login vs auth-error : {Cosine(a, b):F3}");   // expect HIGH (~0.7+)
Console.WriteLine($"login vs banana     : {Cosine(a, c):F3}");   // expect LOW  (~0.1)

// Cosine similarity = dot product / (magnitude * magnitude)
static float Cosine(float[] x, float[] y)
{
    float dot = 0, magX = 0, magY = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < x.Length; i++)
    {
        dot  += x[i] * y[i];
        magX += x[i] * x[i];
        magY += y[i] * y[i];
    }
    return dot / (MathF.Sqrt(magX) * MathF.Sqrt(magY));
}

The key result: "login failed" scores HIGH against "authentication error" but LOW against "banana bread" —
even though they share zero words. The model understood meaning, not spelling.
Keyword search (string.Contains) could never connect those two. Embeddings do.

