Key takeaways:
An embedding = text turned into a vector of numbers that encodes meaning.
Meaning becomes geometry. Similar texts → close vectors; unrelated texts → far apart.
Cosine similarity scores closeness from −1 to 1 (≈1 = same meaning, ≈0 = unrelated).
Use a dedicated embedding model (nomic-embed-text), not a chat model like phi3:mini.
Interface swap: chat uses IChatClient; embeddings use IEmbeddingGenerator. Same OllamaApiClient, same packages.
Semantic > keyword. Embeddings match "login failed" to "authentication error" with no shared words — string.Contains never could.
This powers what's next: semantic search, clustering, and RAG (Day 11) are all just measuring distances between vectors.

One-liner:
Embeddings turn text into vectors so that meaning becomes distance —
and once meaning is math, similarity, search, and RAG are just measuring angles.
